# headlook.xrs - the mono screen is HEAD-LOCKED: turning the simulated head must
# NOT move the picture in the eye (the quad lives in VIEW space and turns with
# the head). The captured content bounding box is the same at every yaw, within
# a percent. When head tracking drives the game camera (ROADMAP S1), a second
# sequence asserts the opposite on the CONTENT (the world moves, the screen does
# not); this one stays the rung-1 contract.
#
# Run it in GAMEPLAY (boot.ps1 first), with the game window foregrounded.
reset
head rot 0 0 0
@frames 10
@shot look_00
@capassert stats.nonBlackPctL ge 10
head rot 10 0 0
@frames 10
@shot look_10
@capdiff stats.bboxPctL 1
@capdiff stats.bboxPctR 1
head rot 25 0 0
@frames 10
@shot look_25
@capdiff stats.bboxPctL 1
@capdiff stats.bboxPctR 1
head rot 45 0 0
@frames 10
@shot look_45
@capdiff stats.bboxPctL 1
@capdiff stats.bboxPctR 1
head rot 0 0 0
